1. W906-PLCLOST: after a PLC link loss golden keeps the last frame (doors / EMG read "closed"; the clear block is commented out, Ken 20250428) and bCheckPLCConnet only notices once the socket is down. MyPLC_IO_Modbus.cpp EOF W906_SafePlcLinkLost = SafePlcIO=1 and (socket down or no reply frame for 2 s, counted from the first ask); W906_SafePlcFrameMark on every taken frame (same line). csystem.cpp DoSystem (inside SystemStart, after golden's G12, on the old blank line): lost -> ShowErrorMessage("WAR16155", K_RETRY, MMSystem), SystemStart=false, StopAllMotor. Door / EMG data untouched. The G23 comment claiming a silent PLC is still caught is marked wrong (same line). tests/test_myplc_modbus.cpp [7]: 74/74.
2. W906-TRAYZ-PITCH-2: the 12 HT9050 Tray Z typed rows (pitch / lift / probe start / probe limit) are TECH_PARA rows, so a hand-made WS teachGo btn=btnGoTZ9050LoaderPitch drove MLoaderZ to the pitch value. MotorAccessResolveTeachButton refuses them (same line; EOF W906_TeachTypedOnly). test_web_motor_access: 1097/1097.
3. W906-IOFIX-2: with the IO thread stuck, the Motor Test page's 100 ms SetTorqueFocusAxis went through RunSync whose freeze clock started at the request -> 5 s stall per beat. Pci1203Monitor.cpp: g_w906IoHeartAt (heartbeat tick), RunSync refuses at once when the heartbeat is already frozen >= 5 s (one line per 50), the wait's freeze clock starts at the last heartbeat, cleared when the thread starts. No test reaches it (needs the card); compiled.

Debug + release (affected targets). Web part (WAR16155 text) in the web commit of the same name. WORKLOG section 2 row 142.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
